        "execSummary":  "Kier Group\u0027s deployment is a useful enterprise case study because it demonstrates the soft-skills dimension of AI adoption: the breakthrough came not from technology but from peer-led learning sessions that made executives and frontline workers comfortable experimenting side by side. For enterprise leaders, the key takeaway is that adoption curve management — not tooling — is often the primary obstacle, and grassroots enablement programs can unlock broad deployment faster than top-down mandates. The developing agent layer for safety and risk analysis also signals that Kier sees Copilot as a platform, not just a productivity add-on. Caveat: the article is a Microsoft-produced customer story, so outcome metrics are self-reported and not independently verified.",
