        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s Connected Apps expansion is a direct move to make Gemini the orchestration hub for enterprise workflows — essentially a conversational layer that can reach into project management, design, and business tools simultaneously. For enterprise operations and customer support leaders, this is significant because it mirrors the agent-orchestration architecture that vendors like Microsoft and Salesforce are building, and it lowers the integration barrier for teams already using tools like Airtable or monday.com. The key strategic question is whether enterprises will trust a consumer-tier Google app as an orchestration layer for sensitive business workflows, or whether they will demand the stricter data governance of Google Cloud\u0027s Vertex AI agents. The announcement lacks specifics on enterprise-grade controls, data handling, and rollout timeline consistency across regions.",
