        "summary":  "Claude Sonnet 5.5 delivers outputs 30% faster and at up to 30% lower cost per task compared to its predecessor while maintaining the same pricing structure. Coding capability improved dramatically, with Terminal-Bench 4.0 scores jumping from 10.3% to 70.6%. The model is optimized for well-scoped knowledge work, document creation, and collaborative workflows.",
        "execSummary":  "Sonnet 5.5\u0027s 30% speed and cost improvement at no price increase is a meaningful efficiency gain for enterprises running Claude at scale — particularly in high-throughput scenarios like customer support automation, document processing, or real-time agentic workflows where latency and cost-per-call compound quickly. The leap in coding benchmark performance (10.3% to 70.6% on Terminal-Bench 4.0) positions Sonnet 5.5 as a credible default for developer tooling and code-assistance workflows that do not require the full weight of Opus. For enterprise architects, this means the mid-tier model now covers a much wider range of production use cases, potentially reducing the need to route tasks to the more expensive Opus tier. The caveat is that benchmark improvements do not always translate uniformly to proprietary enterprise tasks — real-world evaluation against actual workflows remains essential before rebalancing tier routing.",
